GET /session or action status returns the shared collaboration snapshot. POST /session decodes a bounded strict SessionRequest. An omitted action means status; a new participant's omitted kind means human.
Create the ordinary CollaborationSession once through the rooted workspace. Reuse it by reading workspace state through the inspection control lane, so ordinary participant actions do not queue behind legacy evaluation.
Join validates a nonempty name up to 80 bytes and human/agent kind, creates a separate scratch workspace, records attribution and returns participantId/workspaceId.
Publish/unpublish validate a nonempty publication label up to 120 bytes, active participant, typed value and exact nonnegative expectedRevision; invoke the serialized Session operation and return a fresh snapshot even on revision conflict.
Bind validates a variable name, prepares a retained transfer in the Session, writes the variable outside the Session mailbox, then releases the transfer. A busy participant workspace cannot block other session operations.
Note validates nonempty text up to 2000 bytes and active membership, then appends attributed activity. Leave marks inactive and releases the scratch workspace reference.
Return participant/workspace IDs and readable error text with every appropriate response. Participant identity provides attribution, not access control.
participantWorkspace resolves the independent workspace or, if participantId is absent, preserves the existing legacy workspace.
sessionRecord adds participant ID/name, action, detail and UTC timestamp to the shared log.
